doctype html
html
    head

        title= title

        meta(name='viewport' content='width=device-width, minimum-scale=1.0, initial-scale=1.0')
        meta(charset='utf-8')
        link(rel='icon', href='/favicon.ico')

        link(rel='stylesheet', href='/stylesheets/framework/basic.css')
        link(rel='stylesheet', href='/stylesheets/framework/colors.css')
        link(rel='stylesheet', href='/stylesheets/framework/fonts.css')
        link(rel='stylesheet', href='/stylesheets/framework/setup.css')
        link(rel='stylesheet', href='/stylesheets/framework/i18n.css')

        script(src='/javascripts/libs/jquery-3.6.1.min')

        script.
            theme='#{theme}'
            window.PLMX_I18N_DEFAULT='#{uiLanguage}'

        script(src='/i18n/dictionaries.js')
        script(src='/javascripts/framework/i18n.js')
        script(src='/javascripts/framework/setup.js')

    body

        #wrapper.surface-level-2

            #header
                #header-title Setup Wizard
                #header-subtitle Connect this server to your Fusion Manage tenant. Nothing has to be edited by hand.
                #header-state
                #header-profile.field-hint

            #layout

                #steps
                    .step(data-step='1')
                        .step-number 1
                        .step-label Create your APS app
                    .step(data-step='2')
                        .step-number 2
                        .step-label Connect
                    .step(data-step='3')
                        .step-number 3
                        .step-label Preferences
                    .step(data-step='4')
                        .step-number 4
                        .step-label Optional advanced
                    .step(data-step='5')
                        .step-number 5
                        .step-label Test and discover
                    .step(data-step='6')
                        .step-number 6
                        .step-label Save and restart

                #panels

                    .panel(data-step='1')

                        h1 Create your APS app

                        p This server signs you in to Fusion Manage through an Autodesk Platform Services application. You only have to create it once, and you can do it yourself in about two minutes.

                        ol
                            li
                                | Open the
                                a#link-aps(href='https://aps.autodesk.com/myapps/create' target='_blank' rel='noopener')  APS application creation page
                                |  and sign in with your Autodesk account.
                            li
                                | Choose the application type
                                span.emphasis  Desktop, Mobile, Single-Page App
                                | . This type cannot be changed later, so please pick it carefully.
                            li Give the app any name you like, for example "Fusion Manage UX Server".
                            li Paste the callback URL below into the field named Callback URL. It has to match character by character.
                            li Create the app, then copy its Client ID. You will paste it in the next step.

                        .field-block
                            .field-label Callback URL to paste into your APS app
                            .field-row
                                input#callback-display.readonly(type='text' readonly='readonly')
                                .button#copy-callback Copy
                            .field-hint This value is built from the address this server is listening on. You can change it in the next step if port 8080 is already taken on your machine.

                        h2 Whitelist the Client ID in Fusion Manage

                        p Your tenant only accepts logins from Client IDs an administrator has approved. Open the general settings of your tenant, find the list of allowed Client IDs (it can also be labelled Forge Client IDs or APS Client IDs) and add the Client ID of the app you just created.

                        .field-block
                            .field-row
                                a#link-settings.button.disabled(target='_blank' rel='noopener') Open the General Settings of my tenant
                            .field-hint#hint-settings Enter your tenant name in the next step to activate this link.

                        .panel-buttons
                            .button.primary(data-goto='2') Next

                    .panel(data-step='2')

                        h1 Connect

                        p These two values are all this server needs to reach your tenant.

                        .field-block
                            .field-label Tenant
                            input#tenant(type='text' placeholder='mytenant' spellcheck='false' autocomplete='off')
                            .field-hint You can type the short name, for example mytenant, or paste the full address https://mytenant.autodeskplm360.net. The wizard keeps the short name.
                            .field-error#error-tenant

                        .field-block
                            .field-label Client ID
                            input#client-id(type='text' placeholder='Paste the Client ID of your APS app' spellcheck='false' autocomplete='off')
                            .field-hint This is the Client ID from step 1. It is not a password and it is stored in plain text in your connection settings.
                            .field-error#error-client-id

                        .field-block
                            .field-label Callback URL
                            input#redirect-uri(type='text' spellcheck='false' autocomplete='off')
                            .field-hint Leave this as it is unless port 8080 is already used by another program. It has to end with /callback and it has to be identical to the Callback URL of your APS app.
                            .field-error#error-redirect-uri

                        .panel-buttons
                            .button(data-goto='1') Back
                            .button.primary#next-connect(data-goto='3') Next

                    .panel(data-step='3')

                        h1 Preferences

                        .field-block
                            .field-label Default theme
                            select#default-theme
                                option(value='light') Light
                                option(value='dark') Dark
                                option(value='black') Black
                                option(value='fusion') Fusion
                            .field-hint Every user can still switch the theme by adding &theme=light to any address.

                        .field-block
                            .field-label User interface language
                            select#ui-language
                                option(value='') Follow the browser language
                                option(value='en') English
                                option(value='ja') 日本語
                                option(value='ko') 한국어
                            .field-hint This becomes the default language of the user interface for everybody using this server.

                        .panel-buttons
                            .button(data-goto='2') Back
                            .button.primary(data-goto='4') Next

                    .panel(data-step='4')

                        h1 Optional advanced settings

                        p You can safely skip this whole step. Everything here stays empty for most installations.

                        .disclosure#disclosure-advanced
                            .disclosure-title#toggle-advanced Show the optional settings
                            .disclosure-content#content-advanced

                                h2 Second APS app for the admin utilities

                                p
                                    | Two of the applications on this server work on behalf of other people: the
                                    span.emphasis  Outstanding Work Report
                                    | , which lists the open tasks of everybody, and the
                                    span.emphasis  User Settings Manager
                                    | , which copies saved workspace views from one user to other users. Every other application here runs without anything on this page.

                                p
                                    | To act as somebody else, this server has to sign in as itself instead of as you. That needs a
                                    span.emphasis  second APS app
                                    | , in addition to the one you created in step 1, and it has to be of a type which issues a Client Secret. The app from step 1 is of a type that has no Client Secret at all, so it cannot be reused here.

                                p
                                    span.emphasis Please read this before you fill it in.
                                    |  A Client Secret lets this server read and write as any user of your tenant, without that user ever logging in.

                                p Please only provide it while you actually use these two utilities, and clear both fields again afterwards.

                                ol
                                    li
                                        | Open the
                                        a#link-aps-admin(href='https://aps.autodesk.com/myapps/create' target='_blank' rel='noopener')  APS application creation page
                                        |  a second time and sign in with your Autodesk account.
                                    li
                                        | Choose the application type
                                        span.emphasis  Server-to-Server
                                        | . This is the type which issues a Client Secret. This type cannot be changed later, so please pick it carefully.
                                    li Give this app a name which tells it apart from the first one, for example "Fusion Manage UX Admin".
                                    li Create the app, then copy its Client ID and its Client Secret. This is the only moment the Client Secret is shown, so copy it right away.
                                    li Add this second Client ID to the allowed Client IDs of your tenant as well, in the same general settings you used in step 1.
                                    li Paste both values below and let the wizard test them.

                                .field-block
                                    .field-label Admin Client ID
                                    input#admin-client-id(type='text' placeholder='Paste the Client ID of your second APS app' spellcheck='false' autocomplete='off')
                                    .field-hint This is the Client ID of the second app. It must be a different value than the Client ID in step 2.
                                    .field-error#error-admin-client-id

                                .field-block
                                    .field-label Admin Client Secret
                                    input#admin-client-secret(type='password' autocomplete='new-password')
                                    .field-hint Treat this like a password. It is written to your connection settings file and is never sent back to this page again.
                                    .field-error#error-admin-client-secret

                                .field-block
                                    .field-row
                                        .button#test-admin Test these credentials
                                    .field-hint The wizard asks Autodesk for a server token with these two values, exactly as the two utilities do. Nothing is saved by the test and the Client Secret is never written to the console.
                                    .field-message#result-admin

                                h2 Vault connection

                                p Only needed when you use the Vault and Inventor addins of this server. The standard applications never talk to Vault.

                                .field-block
                                    .field-label Vault Gateway
                                    input#vault-gateway(type='text' spellcheck='false' autocomplete='off')
                                    .field-error#error-vault-gateway

                                .field-block
                                    .field-label Vault Name
                                    input#vault-name(type='text' spellcheck='false' autocomplete='off')
                                    .field-error#error-vault-name

                        .panel-buttons
                            .button(data-goto='3') Back
                            .button.primary(data-goto='5') Next

                    .panel(data-step='5')

                        h1 Test and discover

                        h2 Is the tenant reachable?

                        p This only checks that the address of your tenant exists and answers. It does not sign you in yet.

                        .field-block
                            .field-row
                                .button#check-tenant Check the tenant address
                            .field-message#result-tenant

                        h2 Which workspaces does your tenant have?

                        p The applications need the numeric id of each workspace, for example the id of your Items workspace. The wizard reads the list of workspaces from your tenant and matches it against the names the applications expect. Reading that list requires you to be signed in.

                        .field-block
                            .field-row
                                .button#sign-in Sign in to Autodesk
                                .button.primary#discover Discover workspaces
                            .field-message#result-auth
                            .field-message#result-discover

                        #workspace-table

                        .panel-buttons
                            .button(data-goto='4') Back
                            .button.primary(data-goto='6') Next

                    .panel(data-step='6')

                        h1 Save and restart

                        p The wizard writes your answers into the connection settings and the workspace ids into the settings file. A timestamped backup of every file it overwrites is kept next to the original.

                        #summary

                        .field-block
                            .field-label Where should this be saved?
                            .field-row
                                input#save-mode-current(type='radio' name='save-mode' value='current' checked='checked')
                                label(for='save-mode-current') Update the settings this server is running on
                            .field-hint Use this while you are completing or correcting the settings of the tenant you are working with. The server restarts by itself and comes back on the new settings.
                            .field-row
                                input#save-mode-profile(type='radio' name='save-mode' value='profile')
                                label(for='save-mode-profile') Save as a new tenant profile
                            .field-hint A tenant profile keeps a second tenant next to this one, and the list further down lets you switch between them at any time. Saving a profile changes nothing about the tenant this server runs on right now, and the server does not restart.

                        #profile-block

                            .field-block
                                .field-label Name of the tenant profile
                                input#profile-name(type='text' placeholder='tokyo-demo' spellcheck='false' autocomplete='off')
                                .field-hint Letters a to z, digits, dashes and underscores only. It becomes the name of two files and the entry you pick in the list below, so a name like tokyo-demo or customer-abc reads well there.
                                .field-error#error-profile-name

                            .field-message#profile-workspaces

                            .field-block
                                .field-label Tenant profiles on this server
                                #profile-list

                        .field-block
                            .field-row
                                .button.primary#save Save and restart
                            .field-message#result-save

                        #restart-info

                        .panel-buttons
                            .button(data-goto='5') Back
